{
  "_comment": "SYNTHETIC test cases for M-02 parser m02-text-parser/1. Not DrugBank content, no clinical meaning. Expected results written from RULES.md before implementation.",
  "author": "author-half-life",
  "ambiguities": [
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] <exactly 1000 characters whose last sentence ends with '.'> The half-life is 8 hours.", "why": "RULES 1/8: 1000 chars = possible truncation, but 'stored_text_possibly_truncated' on other measurements is only stated for the case where the last sentence lacks terminal punctuation; unclear whether measurements are flagged (and derived blocked) when the 1000-char text ends cleanly."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life is 10 hours in patients aged 65 years.", "why": "'65 years' is a duration excluded by 'aged'; with two durations the sentence is split at the midpoint, so it is unclear whether population 'aged 65 years' lands in the window of the 10-hour value (case kept below without population assertions)."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life varies from 2 hours to 3 days.", "why": "Original 'unit exactly as written' is a single string; RULES does not say which unit (or combined form) is stored for a mixed-unit range (case kept below without unit assertion)."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life is two hours.", "why": "RULES 5.5 defines 'strong keyword' only for Tmax; unclear whether a half-life keyword with only a word-number must yield 'keyword_without_parsable_value' (case kept below without reason-code assertion)."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life is 6 hours every day / prolonged by 2 hours / aged 65 years.", "why": "RULES 5 says excluded durations go to review 'with a reason code' but names no code for every/for/by/age/after exclusions; such cases are kept without reason-code assertions."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life is about 4 hours. Another report gives 4 hours.", "why": "RULES 8 compares 'kind, lower, upper, point' for conflicts; unclear whether differing 'approximate' flags with the same number count as different values."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life is 5 hours [SYNTHETIC].", "why": "RULES 7 shows tokens like [A123]/[L45, T6]; unclear whether a bracketed all-letter word such as [SYNTHETIC] is an inline reference token. Reference cases below therefore put the referenced value in a later sentence."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] The half-life is over 24 hours.", "why": "RULES 4 sends 'over' to review (ambiguous_qualifier) but whether that is a review item only or a review-flagged measurement is not stated explicitly; this file follows RULES header 'either structured or kept as text for review' => review item, no measurement (case kept)."}
  ],
